{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-3","title":"prop:dc-ch7-2-3","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.md","line":40,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex#prop:dc-ch7-2-3","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-2]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#thm:dc-ch3-3-7]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","label":"prop:dc-ch7-2-3","line":56,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Completeness prevents extension]\n\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch7-2-3}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-1, def:dc-ch7-2-2, lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push, thm:dc-ch3-3-7}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.3}\nIf $M$ is complete then $M$ is non-extendible.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-1, def:dc-ch7-2-2, lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push, thm:dc-ch3-3-7}\n\\sketch If $M$ were isometric to a proper open subset of connected $M'$, choose a boundary point and a normal neighborhood there. A geodesic from the boundary point to an interior point restricts, after reversing parameter, to a geodesic in $M$ that cannot be extended to the boundary time, contradicting completeness.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Completeness prevents extension] <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a64632d6368372d322d33\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-2\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-2</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23thm%3Adc-ch3-3-7\">↗ thm:dc-ch3-3-7</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:2.3</span></span>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is complete then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is non-extendible.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-2\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-2</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23thm%3Adc-ch3-3-7\">↗ thm:dc-ch3-3-7</a> \\sketch If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> were isometric to a proper open subset of connected <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M&#x27;$\">$M&#x27;$</span>, choose a boundary point and a normal neighborhood there. A geodesic from the boundary point to an interior point restricts, after reversing parameter, to a geodesic in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> that cannot be extended to the boundary time, contradicting completeness. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-2","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-2"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#thm:dc-ch3-3-7","title":"thm:dc-ch3-3-7","label":"thm:dc-ch3-3-7"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-3","title":"prop:dc-ch7-2-3","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Completeness prevents extension]\n\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch7-2-3}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-1, def:dc-ch7-2-2, lem:dc-ch7-2-3-geodesic-push, thm:dc-ch3-3-7}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.3}\nIf $M$ is complete then $M$ is non-extendible.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begi